SUMMARY:Free Educational and Research Event to Address Breast Cancer and Nanoplastics Learn How to Take "Nano Steps to Reduce Exposures"
DESCRIPTION:Thriving Pink\, in collaboration with the UC Davis Women’s Cancer Care and Research (WeCARE) Program\, is proud to announce a free educational and research event focused on breast cancer and nanoplastics\, taking place Saturday\, October 10\, 2026 in Davis\, CA. \nEVENT DETAILS\nWhat: Breast Cancer & Nanoplastics Educational and Research Event\nWhen: Saturday\, October 10\, 2026\, from 10:30 AM – 12:30 PM\nWhere: Veterans Memorial Center\, 203 E. 14th Street\, Davis\, CA 95616\nCost: Free and open to the public.\nRegistration: www.ThrivingPink.org/nanoplastics (Registration is suggested to save your seat.) \nAre you a breast cancer survivor? You’re invited to stay after the program to take part in a nanoplastics research study with the UC Davis Comprehensive Cancer Center. Study follows presentation at 11:30 AM. As a thank-you for your participation\, you’ll receive a $25 Amazon gift card. \nMaking complex science simple and useful. This program will teach the community how to take “Nano Steps to Reduce Exposures” to nanoplastics\, a growing environmental health concern that has received increasing attention from scientists. The event offers an opportunity for community members to learn directly from experts about practical steps to reduce exposure to these tiny particles. \n“We are excited to bring this important information and research opportunity to our community\,” said Denise Rose\, Board Chair of Thriving Pink. “Understanding the connection between environmental exposures and breast cancer is important for prevention. This event gives people useful knowledge they can use every day.” \nAdditional events are scheduled for November 7\, 2026 in Woodland (en Español) and January 2027 in West Sacramento\, bringing this important health information to more communities across the region. \nStay curious. Stay informed. Take action. \nAbout UC Davis Women’s Cancer Care and Research (WeCARE) Program\nThe UC Davis WeCARE Program is committed to advancing women’s cancer care through innovative research\, comprehensive patient care\, and community education. As part of the UC Davis Comprehensive Cancer Center\, WeCARE brings together leading researchers and clinicians to improve outcomes for women facing cancer. https://health.ucdavis.edu/cancer/ \nAbout Thriving Pink\nThriving Pink is a volunteer-driven 501(c)(3) nonprofit and the leading organization in Yolo County supporting those impacted by breast cancer. Through evidence-based programs and community partnerships\, we provide a compassionate network of support and empower individuals with the knowledge and resources to reduce their breast cancer risk. Learn more at www.ThrivingPink.org.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/free-educational-and-research-event-to-address-breast-cancer-and-nanoplastics-learn-how-to-take-nano-steps-to-reduce-exposures/
LOCATION:Veterans Memorial Center\, Multipurpose Room\, 203 E. 14th Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Nanoplastics-Event-101026-Instagram.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Thriving Pink":MAILTO:emily.spencer@thrivingpink.org
GEO:38.556688;-121.7477363
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Veterans Memorial Center Multipurpose Room 203 E. 14th Street Davis CA 95616 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Multipurpose Room\, 203 E. 14th Street:geo:-121.7477363,38.556688
END:VEVENT
